item.description:
GET /v1/live is a WebSocket (server built with --features live) and cannot be sent as an HTTP request here. Use Postman's WebSocket request type: connect to ws://localhost:3000/v1/live, send the GaiseLiveConfig JSON as the first text frame, then GaiseLiveInput frames. First frame example:

{
  "model": "openai::gpt-realtime-2.1",
  "system_instruction": "You are a concise voice assistant.",
  "modalities": [
    "text",
    "audio"
  ],
  "voice": "alloy",
  "transcription": {
    "input": true,
    "output": true
  }
}

Then: {"type":"text","text":"Hello"} … {"type":"close"}. Protocol: wiki/api.md#get-v1live and wiki/examples.md#live--realtime.
